      "problem": "What is $\\frac{3t+6}{4t+8}$ reduced to its lowest terms?",
      "worked_solution": "We factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any factors that they have in common.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3t+6}{4t+8} & =\\frac{3\\cdot (t+2)}{4\\cdot (t+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot \\cancel{(t+2)}}{4\\cdot \\cancel{(t+2)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
